[[Orbs]] are a mechanic used by [[The Defect]].

== Mechanics ==
'''Orbs''' have two abilities each, a '''Passive''' effect that happens every turn, and an '''Evoke''' effect.

=== Orb Slots ===
Using Orbs requires you have '''Orb Slots'''. Each slot can hold one Orb.

Orb Slots follow a first-in, first-out structure. Visually, Orbs are both Channeled and Evoked in right-to left order, with Orbs shifting right to fill any empty slots.

You can have a maximum of 10 Orb Slots at once.

{{R|Prismatic Shard}}, as well as the {{KW|Diverse}} and {{KW|Blue Cards}} modifiers, will add an Orb Slot to any character that is not the [[Defect]].

=== Channel ===
When an Orb is '''Channeled''', it is placed into the right-most available Orb Slot. If all Orb Slots are occupied, the right-most Orb is Evoked, making space for the newly Channeled Orb.

=== Evoke ===
When an Orb is '''Evoked''', it is removed from its Slot (allowing Orbs behind it to move forward), and its Evoke effect is activated.

=== Passive ===
Each Orb type has a '''Passive''' ability which is activated automatically once per turn. {{KW|Lightning}}, {{KW|Frost}}, and {{KW|Dark}} Orbs activate their Passives at end of turn, while {{KW|Plasma}} Orbs activate theirs at the beginning of your turn.

== Orb Types ==
There are four types of Orbs.

=== Lightning Orbs ===
{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}
{{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} are the most common damage dealing Orbs. Their Passive effect deals 3 damage to a random enemy at end of turn. When Evoked, they instead do 8 damage to a random enemy.

Lightning is the most common Orb type, having the most cards which Channel it, as well as being generated by both the Defect's starter relic, {{R|Cracked Core}}, and one of its Basics, {{C|Zap}}. It also has the most support of the Orb types, with {{C|Thunder Strike}} scaling based on how many Lightning you've Channeled this combat, as well as {{C|Electrodynamics}} making Lightning Orbs damage all enemies.

=== Frost Orbs ===
{{Keyword Infobox|Frost}}
{{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} are the {{KW|Block}} generating Orbs. Their Passive effect gives 2 {{KW|Block}} at end of turn, while the Evoke effect gives 5 {{KW|Block}}.

Frost is the second most common Orb type, being generated by nearly as many sources as {{KW|Lightning}}.
{{Clear}}
=== Dark Orbs ===
{{Keyword Infobox|Dark}}
{{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} are the other type of damage dealing Orbs, with an emphasis on scaling. Dark Orbs have a damage value, which starts at 6 when Channeled. Their Passive adds 6 to their damage value at end of turn, while their Evoke ability deals the damage value to the enemy with the lowest current HP.

If multiple enemies have the lowest HP, the left-most enemy is chosen first.

Dark Orbs are much less common than {{KW|Lightning}} and {{KW|Frost}} Orbs, and generally require a different approach. While the other Orb types have similar effects for their Passive and Evoked abilities, Dark Orbs do very little if Evoked before applying their Passive, and benefit from their Passive ability being used before Evoking.

=== Plasma Orbs ===
{{Keyword Infobox|Plasma}}
{{KW|Plasma|Plasma Orbs}} are the {{Icon|BE}} Energy generating Orbs. Their Passive generates 1 {{Icon|BE}} at the start of the turn, while Evoking them generates 2 {{Icon|BE}} instead. Unlike the other Orb types, Plasma Orbs are wholly unaffected by {{BD|Focus}}.

Plasma orbs are decidedly the least common Orb type. Given how differently they work from the other Orb types, they are able to synergize with things the other Orbs do not, perhaps due to reducing {{BD|Focus}}.

